LATENCY_OFFSET: 1

**Metric targeted:** Timing (the design VIOLATES its constraint: worst slack -1.3 ns, max frequency only 289.9 MHz). This is priority #1 per the diagnosis rules, and the critical path (43 levels of logic, startpoint _96725_ to endpoint _94933_) runs through the explicitly-flagged "unbalanced chain of conditional adds" (`d0` through `d9`) that feeds the `acc` register. A prior attempt to reassociate/rebalance this same chain into a tree could not be verified in time (checker timeout), so this time I use a structural pipeline insertion instead of any arithmetic reassociation.

**Change (pipeline insertion, not reassociation):**
Split the existing 9-stage dependent chain `d0 → d1 → … → d9` exactly at its midpoint, between `d4` and `d5` (i.e., after the `state[4]`-conditioned add and before the `state[5]`-conditioned add). Concretely:

1. Add a new register stage `d4_r` that captures `d4` on every clock edge (no arithmetic change — it is the same `d4` expression already in the RTL).
2. Add companion pipeline registers that capture, in the same cycle as `d4_r`, the exact operands the second half of the chain needs: `held_r <= held`, `lenx_r <= lenx`, `cntx_r <= cntx`, `ext_r <= ext`, and one-cycle-delayed copies of the state bits used by stages 5–9 (`state5_r <= state[5]` is not needed since `d4` already consumed it; keep delayed copies of `state[8]`, `state[9]`, `state[10]`, `state[11]`).
3. Rebuild `d5` through `d9` unchanged in arithmetic form, but sourced from `d4_r`, `held_r`, `lenx_r`, `cntx_r`, `ext_r`, and the delayed state bits instead of the original combinational signals.
4. The `acc` register update (`acc <= d9` when the delayed `in_valid_r` is set) now consumes this second-stage result one cycle later than before; likewise gate `out_data <= acc`, `out_valid <= state[12]`, and `status <=` with the same one-cycle-delayed pipeline so every downstream consumer of the split chain sees a consistently-staged value.

This breaks the single 43-level combinational path into two roughly-equal ~21-level combinational stages separated by a register, which is expected to bring arrival time under the 1.99 ns required time. Because the second half of the accumulate chain now completes one clock cycle later than in the original RTL, the module produces its accumulation-dependent outputs (`out_valid`, `out_data`, `status`) one cycle later end-to-end than the baseline, hence LATENCY_OFFSET: 1.
